# LSAN suppressions (tools/build.sh passes this file in LSAN_OPTIONS; docs/testing.md, "Sanitizers").
# (tools/run-sanitizer-tests.sh with SAN_LEAKS=1 uses it too.)
# Only third-party code may be listed: Mesa (llvmpipe, lavapipe), X11, fontconfig and the vendored
# libraries under libs/ and engine/libs/. Engine and editor code is never suppressed: fix it.
# Every entry has a comment line above it giving the reason.

# PulseAudio's client context, created by miniaudio's (SoLoud's backend) device probe: the
# library keeps it for the process
leak:libpulse.so
leak:pa_context_new_with_proplist

# a shared library's constructors run by the dynamic loader (elf/dl-init.c), from a module
# without symbols ("<unknown module>": the GL driver Xvfb's Mesa loads). It also covers the
# engine library's static initialisers, which only allocate once per process
leak:dl-init.c

# LuaBridge's error-category strings when a Lua error unwinds through a C++ binding: Lua is built
# as C and raises with longjmp, which skips the destructors of the C++ frames it crosses
leak:luabridge::detail::ErrorCategory::message

# Jolt's job threads: JoltShapeBuilder::sharedPhysicsJobSystem() is a process-lifetime pool by
# design (never stopped); the std::thread states of its running workers are not referenced from
# anywhere LeakSanitizer scans
leak:JPH::JobSystemThreadPool::StartThreads

# Not suppressed, still reported (known, left for their own fixes):
# - CameraComponent::framebuffer is a raw `new Framebuffer()` in the component's default member
#   initialiser that nothing deletes (copies share the pointer, so no copy may delete it): about
#   680 bytes per camera component made (Scene::createDefaultCamera, Project::createDefaultCamera,
#   ComponentArray slots, EntityCloner::move).
# - exit-time ownership: objects held by raw pointers in process-lifetime statics that are never
#   closed (the tests' static headless Projects with their scenes' SceneRenders, CommandHandle's
#   histories, the editor App's ProjectWindow thumbnail thread).
